  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="hw05-q1">
      <title>Question 1: Polynomial, Step, and Spline Models</title>

      <introduction>
        <p>
          Use the <c>polynomial-toydata.csv</c> data set from the course
          website. Predict <c>y</c> from <c>x</c> using polynomial regression,
          a step function, and a cubic spline. For each model, identify its
          tuning parameter, select it with <m>k</m>-fold cross-validation,
          and refit the selected model on all observations. Finally, overlay
          the three fits on one plot and compare them.
        </p>
        <p>
          The original notebook generated the toy data as follows. Use the
          published CSV for your analysis.
        </p>
        <program language="python">
          <code>
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

np.random.seed(42)
f_true = lambda x: (x + 2) * (x - 2) * (x + 6) * x + 20
x_data = np.random.uniform(-6, 3, 100)
y_data = f_true(x_data) + np.random.normal(0, 10, size=x_data.shape)
toy_data = pd.DataFrame({"x": x_data, "y": y_data})
          </code>
        </program>
        <program language="python">
          <preamble visible="true">
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
from sklearn.model_selection import KFold, cross_val_score
from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline
from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeatures, KBinsDiscretizer, SplineTransformer
          </preamble>
          <code>
url = "https://msu-cmse-courses.github.io/CMSE381-S26/_downloads/f642ded4bf0e8536ccd7675bb8d41449/polynomial-toydata.csv"
polydf = pd.read_csv(url, index_col=0)
X = polydf[["x"]].to_numpy()
y = polydf["y"].to_numpy()
t_plot = np.linspace(-6, 3, 400).reshape(-1, 1)
          </code>
        </program>
      </introduction>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-poly-i" workspace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (A-i) For polynomial regression, identify the tuning parameter.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-poly-ii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (A-ii) Use <m>k</m>-fold cross-validation to select a polynomial
            degree. Report the candidate degrees and validation errors.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-poly-iii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (A-iii) Refit polynomial regression on all observations using
            the selected degree.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-step-i" workspace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (B-i) For the step-function model, identify the tuning parameter.
            State whether you count intervals or interior cutpoints.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-step-ii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (B-ii) Use <m>k</m>-fold cross-validation to choose the number of
            intervals or cutpoints. Report the candidates and validation
            errors. Learn the interval boundaries separately within each
            training fold.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-step-iii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (B-iii) Refit the step-function model on all observations using
            the selected number of intervals or cutpoints.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-spline-i" workspace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (C-i) For a cubic spline, identify the tuning parameter.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-spline-ii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (C-ii) Use <m>k</m>-fold cross-validation to select the number
            of spline knots. Report the candidates and validation errors.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-spline-iii">
        <statement>
          <p>
            (C-iii) Refit the cubic spline on all observations using the
            selected number of knots.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-plot">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Plot the observed data and all three fitted models together.
            Label the three fitted curves or steps.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q1-compare" workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Compare the three fits. Which model would you select, and why?
            Support your answer with both the plot and the
            cross-validation results.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="hw05-q2-step">
      <title>Question 2(A): A Step-Function Basis</title>
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Consider a step function with two interior cutpoints at
          <m>c_1=3</m> and <m>c_2=7</m>.
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q2-step-i" workspace="2in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Write equations for the three basis functions
            <m>C_0(x)</m>, <m>C_1(x)</m>, and <m>C_2(x)</m>.
            Sketch all three, showing their values on the intervals
            separated by 3 and 7.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q2-step-ii" workspace="2in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Sketch the learned function
            <m>f(x)=\beta_0+\beta_1C_1(x)+\beta_2C_2(x)</m>
            when <m>\beta_0=2</m>, <m>\beta_1=3</m>, and
            <m>\beta_2=-1</m>. Label its value on each interval.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>

  <page>
    <exercise xml:id="hw05-q2-spline">
      <title>Question 2(B): A Cubic Spline with One Knot</title>
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Consider a cubic spline with a knot at <m>c_1=4</m>.
          Its basis functions are
          <m>b_1(x)=x</m>, <m>b_2(x)=x^2</m>,
          <m>b_3(x)=x^3</m>, and <m>b_4(x)=h(x,4)</m>, where
          <m>h(x,4)=(x-4)^3</m> for <m>x>4</m> and
          <m>h(x,4)=0</m> otherwise. The learned model is
          <m>f(x)=3+b_1(x)-2b_2(x)+3b_3(x)-4b_4(x)</m>.
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q2-spline-i">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Write the equation of <m>f(x)</m> as a piecewise polynomial
            on either side of <m>x=4</m>. Draw its graph.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q2-spline-ii" workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What conditions must a piecewise polynomial satisfy to be
            a cubic spline?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw05-q2-spline-iii" workspace="2in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Check that the function from part (i) satisfies those
            conditions at <m>x=4</m>.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>
